  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "The number of views $V,$ in millions, of a viral video after $t$ days is modeled by $V(t)=\\frac{{10}^{t}}{\\operatorname{ln}\u206110}$ for $0\\le t\\le 6.$ What is the instantaneous rate of change of the number of views as a function of $t?$\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change is\n{{field-1}} views per day.",
  "worked_solution": "The instantaneous rate of change of the number of views is equal to ${V}^{\u2032}(t).$ \n\nFirst, we take the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{V}^{\u2032}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{10}^{t}}{\\operatorname{ln}\u206110}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{10}^{t}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}\u206110}{\\operatorname{ln}\u206110} \\\\  & ={10}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change of the number of views is ${10}^{t}.$",
